A||||11||DR650SE||Paint calipers?||||5||
Z||000000||DR650SE||10-28-2001||12:49 AM||||Can you paint the brake calipers?  I painted the visible side of my engine with red high temp engine paint and had some left over.  I would like to paint the calipers red too to give them that high performace look.  I like the way the red calipers look on the porche but don't want to drop that dime...yet. I read earlier that high temp wouldn't work on the rotor, but is it ok for the caliper.  I dont think it will hurt anything, I just wanted to make sure. Thanks. <P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||10-28-2001||05:38 AM||||It will work. I just use regular auto paint on mine, Its been there for a couple years now.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-28-2001||06:03 AM||||Remember that brake fluid will eat paint.  Not necessarily a problem, but be careful when you're changing lines, etc.<P>Keep in mind that red calipers will only add 5-10hp.  If you paint them yellow, you should see at least a 15hp gain.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DR650SE||10-28-2001||08:54 AM||||Sweet! Extra HP! LOL Thanks||||reg||6
Z||000004||DR650SE||10-28-2001||08:54 AM||||Sweet! Extra HP! LOL Thanks<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||6
Z||000005||FieroBUZZ||10-28-2001||09:29 AM||||I did mine blue, MM.  Do I lose horsepower?<P>Gary<BR>Black 86 GT||||reg||6
Z||000006||FieroLisa||10-28-2001||09:38 AM||||I painted mine purple, I'm scared to know what that means  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I followed Rogers advice and used regular car paint, the exact color I used on my car. Some of it did chip off because I did a shady job of prepping it. But I just did the upgrade to Grand Am so I don't know if I will paint them again or not, they look so nice and new right now...<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000007||Banzai||10-28-2001||09:43 AM||||I painted the calipers on my Z28 red and it held up fine. A buddy of mine painted his mustang calipers red and they also held up fine. We both used regular "rustoleum" rattle can paint.  Do a good job prepping them and the paint will stick and stay. I'll be painting mine (2m4) today.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroBUZZ||10-28-2001||09:49 AM||||Bad news, Lisa....your whole darn car is purple.  LOL<P>Looks great!<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000009||Eric_PA||10-28-2001||10:08 AM||||FieroLisa... If you didn't paint your GA brakes, they will rust real fast. I did that upgrade on my fiero last year and they looked good at first, but after a few months...rust  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I ended up taking them back off and had one heck of a time cleaning them up before painting.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Rick 88||10-28-2001||01:19 PM||||If you add Rodney's "Fiero" decals to you 88 calipers after painting them you will definitely get second looks cruising down the road with an open design wheel! Mine are white emblems on red calipers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Rick <BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||3
Z||000011||DR650SE||10-28-2001||10:44 PM||||Well I just got dine painting Mavericks fingernails a bright red with the engine paint and they look really good.  Anyone who wants to improve the look of thier car with out a lot of $ should do this.  It gives it more of the proformance look.  <P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
